  "question": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>17</mn><mi>mg</mi></math> of a hydrocarbon (M.F. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>16</mn></msub></math>) takes up <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>40</mn><mi>mL</mi></math> of the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;gas measured at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>760</mn><mi>mm</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hg</mi></math>. Ozonolysis of the same hydrocarbon yields</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><munder><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mo>|</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></munder></munder><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo><munder><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mo>|</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></munder></munder><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo><munder><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mo>|</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></munder></munder><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><munder><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mo>|</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></munder></munder><mo>-</mo><munder><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mo>|</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></munder></munder><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math></p><p>The number of double bond/s present in the hydrocarbon is</p>",
